00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:19.960
it doesn’t really matter all that much anyway. All&nbsp;
of Amazon’s investors including Jeff Bezos will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:25.200
just own both companies which could allow them to&nbsp;
grow to even larger heights. None of this is to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:30.080
say that Amazon is destined to be a monopoly&nbsp;
forever though. In fact, Jeff Bezos would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.080 --> 00:13:00.600
the first one to admit that Amazon isn’t gonna&nbsp;
last forever. But monopolies like Amazon aren’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:06.400
taken down by litigation or government action.&nbsp;
Monopolies are a monopoly for a reason. It’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:11.880
not because these companies are so smart or they&nbsp;
have so much power or any of that. It’s because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:17.640
their current value in the marketplace is simply&nbsp;
indispensable. Splitting up such company won’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:23.880
change that. The only way that such monopolies&nbsp;
are destroyed is by an extreme market shift: when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:30.720
the next revolutionary shopping platform comes out&nbsp;
and Amazon is no longer indispensible. Until then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:37.000
any noise like this lawsuit can’t really hurt them&nbsp;
whether it’s successful or not. If anything, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:43.080
just gives them an opportunity to clear their name&nbsp;
and double down. With these types of lawsuits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:47.760
the public is usually rooting against the&nbsp;
big tech company. But, not too long ago,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:52.360
the public was actually rooting for Google to win&nbsp;
a lawsuit. Check out this video to learn more.

